{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpc", "label": "gRPC", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcserveractor", "label": "GrpcServerActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A concrete actor that loads the proto, registers handlers and binds in preStart \u2014 spawn returns before the bind completes. Each method maps to a handler actor keyed by method name; any method absent from the map is reported UNIMPLEMENTED.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcclientactor", "label": "GrpcClientActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Every call names a target actor that receives the reply and any stream frames. withDeadlineMs bounds UNARY calls only: a gRPC deadline covers a whole RPC and one value cannot both fail a request/response call promptly and let a long-lived stream run.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcinbound", "label": "GrpcInbound frame union", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_call_metadata", "label": "Per-call gRPC metadata record", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Because the record holds strings, a header sent more than once collapses to its FIRST value and binary (-bin) headers are omitted entirely. The record has no prototype, so a lookup for a name like `constructor` never succeeds by accident.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcstreamhandle", "label": "GrpcStreamHandle capability token", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "streamId is the correlation id so one collector can multiplex streams; token is the capability. A tell carries no verified sender, so a sequential id would let anything that can reach the client actor write into a stream it never opened \u2014 the token is 64 bits of crypto-grade randomness, which makes the lookup itself the ownership check.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_bidi_in_band_handshake", "label": "Bidi in-band streamId handshake weakness", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Bidi still delivers its streamId as a first stream-data frame whose chunk is { __streamId }. The hint is indistinguishable from real stream data and the id is guessable \u2014 a known weakness tracked as issue #788; the stream-started frame plus capability handle is what it will adopt, so write new code against the client-stream shape.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_streaming_modes", "label": "Four gRPC streaming modes", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Chunks that arrive before a client-stream handler subscribes are held and replayed on the first onData, so nothing is lost in the turn between the call landing in the mailbox and the handler running.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_health_checking", "label": "gRPC health checking", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "There is deliberately no boolean toggle and no HOCON leaf: a health service that answers SERVING unconditionally is worse than none at all, since a Kubernetes probe would keep the pod in rotation straight through an outage. Enabling it requires naming where the status comes from \u2014 passing healthChecksOf(system) IS the opt-in, so the gRPC Check and /ready stay in lockstep by construction.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_healthcheckregistry", "label": "HealthCheckRegistry (healthChecksOf)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One registry per ActorSystem, already carrying the framework's cluster readiness checks. A bare new HealthCheckRegistry() would fork gRPC Check from /ready and only one of the two would be the answer a load balancer acts on.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_tls_credentials", "label": "gRPC TLS credentials", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "TLS is opt-in via withCredentials and defaults to insecure when omitted; certificates are supplied as Uint8Array values, not file paths. Handlers and TLS credentials come through the builder, never HOCON.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpc", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcserveractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/grpc.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpc", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_grpc_grpcclientactor", "relation": 